---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="PMO Lead and automation developer at a professional services firm, working where operations, reporting, and technology meet."
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
      <h1>
        I build the infrastructure that makes a professional services firm run.
      </h1>

      <div class="about__intro">
        <figure class="about__portrait">
          <img
            src="/images/marisol.jpg"
            alt="Marisol Delbrey"
            width="1024"
            height="1280"
          />
        </figure>

        <div class="prose stack">
          <p>
            I'm a PMO Lead and automation developer at a professional services
            firm. My work sits at the intersection of operations, reporting, and
            technology: connecting systems that weren't designed to talk to each
            other, automating processes that run on manual effort, and building
            the data layer that makes both possible.
          </p>

          <p>
            I came up through <a href="https://breakthroughtech.org"
              >Breakthrough Tech AI</a
            >, a competitive fellowship at UCLA, where I did a case competition
            with Accenture and earned a machine learning certification from
            Cornell University. Accenture is where I figured out what I actually
            wanted to do: not technology for its own sake, and not operations
            without the technical depth to change them. The combination is what
            drives the work.
          </p>

          <p>
            Right now I'm building an API connection between our practice
            management system and our collections hub, consolidating billing data
            into a Snowflake layer so reports stop being one-off exports and
            start being a live data product. I'm automating client intake so a
            sold opportunity flows from CRM into the practice management system
            without anyone rekeying it. I'm building an AI chatbot for the firm's
            website and a separate internal one for HR. I'm automating monthly
            balanced scorecards for the full staff. Most of these projects
            started because two systems weren't talking to each other and nobody
            had connected the dots yet. That's usually where I start.
          </p>

          <p>
            The firms I work in run on trust: with clients, with regulators, with
            each other. Automation in that environment has to be reliable,
            auditable, and built with the constraints in mind, not around them. I
            build things that actually run inside real organizations with real
            compliance requirements. That is harder than a demo and more useful
            than a framework.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section about-details">
    <div class="wrap grid grid--2">
      <div>
        <h2 class="eyebrow">Focus areas</h2>
        <ul class="plain-list">
          <li>Project Management Office</li>
          <li>Workflow Automation</li>
          <li>AI Implementation</li>
          <li>Data Reporting and Operations</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="eyebrow">Background</h2>
        <ul class="plain-list">
          <li>PMO Lead, Professional Services Firm, 2025 to present</li>
          <li>Strategy and Technology Intern, Accenture</li>
          <li>
            PMP Candidate (exam target September 2026); Machine Learning
            Certification, Cornell University
          </li>
          <li>B.A. Philosophy, Computer Science Minor, Chapman University</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section about-cta">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="lead">
        If you're working on something at this intersection, I'd like to hear
        about it.
      </p>
      <a class="button button--accent" href="/contact/">Get in touch</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  /* Portrait sits under the heading on phones and beside the copy on desktop.
     It is first in the DOM so it stays next to the heading when stacked. */
  .about__intro {
    display: grid;
    gap: clamp(1.5rem, 4vw, 3rem);
    align-items: start;
  }

  @media (min-width: 52rem) {
    .about__intro {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr 0.6fr;
    }

    .about__portrait {
      grid-column: 2;
      grid-row: 1;
    }
  }

  .about__portrait {
    margin: 0;
  }

  /* Landscape source cropped to portrait; matches the hero framing. */
  .about__portrait img {
    width: 100%;
    aspect-ratio: 4 / 5;
    object-fit: cover;
    object-position: 47% 35%;
    border-radius: 2px;
  }

  .about-details,
  .about-cta {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-rule);
  }

  .plain-list {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .plain-list li {
    padding: 0.6rem 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-rule);
  }

  .about-cta .lead {
    margin-bottom: 1.75rem;
  }
</style>
